{"packet_id":"e00ba7926c05ad68","dimensions":{"problem_framing":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A1"],"reason":"A1 lists four alternatives, including licensing, plus several constraints. The objective restates the question as 'whether there is sufficient evidence' rather than separating the underlying business goal from the proposed consumer product. It does not take up the use-case premise in acr-fr-purpose: PLBs are meant for remote environments after telephone or radio have been exhausted. That premise bears directly on a marine focus but is never raised."},"causal_mechanism":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A9"],"reason":"A9 names a benefit (higher-margin sales, premium pricing). Its behavioural driver, that recreational mariners 'currently lack affordable, reliable emergency communication tools', is asserted as fact with no supporting source. 'Used by friends and family' is not explained. The step to value capture is asserted rather than traced."},"distinct_theories":{"status":"scored","score":0,"event_ids":["A9","A10"],"reason":"T2 (A10) copies T1 (A9) word for word, adding only a trust clause. T1 already lists that trust clause as an assumption. The assumptions and predictions are identical, so these are copies, not rivals."},"assumptions_predictions":{"status":"scored","score":2,"event_ids":["A9","A10"],"reason":"The predictions are observable, for example surveyed purchase intent above $100 and regional sales differences. The $100 intent prediction would trouble the theory if it failed. However, both theories share every prediction, so none of them tells the theories apart. 'Market share measurable within 12 months' is weak."},"evidence_judgement":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A11","A12","A14"],"reason":"Each assessment states what its source does not show, which is useful. However, A12 and A14 label GCN news items as 'independent_study' when the dossier class is verified_observation, so the evidence types are misclassified. All three sources are marked neutral. The trajectory never considers fit to the customer group: the Alaska rescue figure in A14 concerns remote PLB use, not recreational boating."},"seeking_challenge":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A13"],"reason":"A13 runs a search against T1 and retrieves acr-fr-purpose, acr-fr-registration and acr-fr-rent, but none of these is assessed or reported. acr-fr-purpose, which frames the PLB as a last resort for remote use, could challenge the marine use case. It is ignored."},"experiment_design":{"status":"scored","score":1,"event_ids":["A15","A10"],"reason":"A15 compares a family-use frame with a peer-use frame. T2 (A10) says nothing about peer use, so the T2 prediction in A15 is invented and the test cannot separate the stated theories. The decision rule is internally inconsistent: it proceeds at a 20% WTP gap, declines below '10 percentage points' (mixed units), and leaves the gap between those thresholds undefined. It also ties the investment decision to a difference between frames rather than to absolute demand. Treating 'US, Alaska, Hawaii' as separate regions is odd. The cost and sample are assumptions."},"revision":{"status":"not_applicable","score":null,"event_ids":[],"reason":"Revision is excluded from packet.applicable_dimensions, and no update was scheduled or delivered."},"recommendation":{"status":"scored","score":2,"event_ids":["A16","A17"],"reason":"A17 declines to invest yet, citing unknown demand. It commits to a next action and states reversal conditions, and the uncertainty is stated honestly. However, its reversal criterion (absolute WTP above $100) contradicts the frame-difference decision rule in A15. It also rests on a non-discriminating test. The value proposition includes 'peer coordination', which no source supports."}},"red_flags":[{"kind":"non_discriminating_test","event_ids":["A15","A10"],"reason":"The family-versus-peer framing does not correspond to any difference between T1 and T2. T2's 'peer use' prediction is invented, so the test cannot separate the theories."},{"kind":"unsupported_inference","event_ids":["A9","A10"],"reason":"The claim that recreational mariners 'currently lack affordable, reliable emergency communication tools' is stated as fact with no supporting evidence."},{"kind":"unsupported_inference","event_ids":["A12","A14"],"reason":"News excerpts are labelled 'independent_study', which misstates the evidence class."},{"kind":"unsupported_inference","event_ids":["A17"],"reason":"The value proposition claims 'peer coordination' and premium-price value without any source support."},{"kind":"other","event_ids":["A13"],"reason":"The challenge search results are never assessed. acr-fr-purpose, a potential challenge to the marine use case, goes unreported."},{"kind":"other","event_ids":["A15","A17"],"reason":"The decision rules are inconsistent: A15 uses a frame-difference rule with mixed units and an undefined middle band, while A17 uses an absolute $100 rule."}],"suitable_for_training":false,"screen_reason":"The episode is complete but has critical errors. The two theories are duplicates and the proposed test cannot discriminate between them. There are unsupported factual assertions and misclassified evidence. The challenge results go unassessed, and the decision rules are internally inconsistent. Any one of these errors is enough to reject the trajectory."}
